WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.020
- Hey guys, it's Justine
and WWDC 2021 is here.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.320
If you guys watched the event,

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.160
you're probably already
aware of all of the things

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.100
that I'm gonna talk about.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.640
But if you didn't, we're gonna
go through a little recap.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.810
Now WWDC is a developer conference,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.130
which is mostly focusing around software

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.147
and giving developers a heads-up of like,

00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:19.030
"Hey, this is what we have coming out,

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.910
start developing for our platform."

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.230
It is exciting 'cause if you
do have a developer's account

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.130
and you are a developer,

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.530
you will have access to beta
versions of these things.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:31.530
So, I'm just patiently waiting
here for the iOS 15 beta,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.730
the new iPad OS, and of
course, Mac OS Monterey!

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.590
That is the followup
to our current Big Sur.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.590
And I've loved Big Sur so much.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.430
I know I talked about this
in my Predictions Video.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.870
And it's crazy 'cause my
sister and I were discussing

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.700
what we thought the name was gonna be.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.220
And I don't know, we kind of guessed it.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.430
Monterey. I like Monterrey.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.953
Man, we've never been to Mammoth.

00:00:52.953 --> 00:00:53.869
- [Sister] Maybe Tahoe?

00:00:53.869 --> 00:00:55.550
But that's in Nevada, but also California.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.410
- Mac OS Monterrey, oh!

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.650
Let's start with some of the
things that they announced.

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:01.880
Obviously, iOS 15 is something

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.310
that we're all looking forward to.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.590
Because this is setting us up

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.330
for what to expect in the
next version of the iPhone.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.470
So the iPhone 13,

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.300
or whatever it is that
they're gonna be calling it,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.940
will of course be launching with iOS 15.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.350
And the first thing that they talked about

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:15.547
in the keynote was FaceTime.

00:01:15.547 --> 00:01:18.697
And I'm kind of excited about
this because I like FaceTime,

00:01:18.697 --> 00:01:22.420
but there's so many things,
especially over this past year,

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.480
that we've come so accustomed
to being able to do

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.580
in video conferencing.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.730
And of course that's being
able to share a link out

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.890
and anybody being able to view it,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.460
whether you're on an
Android, or a Mac, or a PC.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.190
And even be able to share
what's on your screen.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.480
There'll be so many times
that you're doing a FaceTime

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.420
and you have to click off.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.690
You wanna share a link,
you send it in iMessages.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:44.310
But now you can actually
do FaceTime screen-sharing

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.193
which is really cool.

00:01:45.193 --> 00:01:47.040
They also wanted FaceTime audio

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.160
to be a little bit more
natural and conversational,

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:53.030
so they announced Spacial
Audio and Voice Isolation.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.030
And they also have the option of switching

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.130
from voice isolation to wide spectrum.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.380
And with that, that'll pick up
all of the sound around you.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.430
With voice isolation,

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.367
that's just gonna be doing
just that: isolating your voice

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.540
(chuckles) and just ignoring
the sounds around you.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.850
They have a new grid layout

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.170
which will highlight
anytime anybody is talking,

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.180
which is nice, also very common,

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.090
so I'm glad that they are
bringing that to FaceTime.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.780
Portrait Mode Video,
having that beautiful BOCA,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.980
which this is a beautiful BOCA

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.630
because I'm using a very expensive camera

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:22.560
and a very expensive 1.4 F-stop lens.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.430
But with portrait mode

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.650
and being able to use the
LIDAR and depth sensing,

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.140
you're able to mimic this sort of a look.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.040
So I think that's gonna
be really cool to do

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.120
in your FaceTime videos.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.090
But the one thing that
I'm so excited about

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.580
is FaceTime links.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.140
So you're gonna be able to
schedule your FaceTime calls

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.570
and send out a link to
your friends, or family,

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.140
or whoever it is that you're
gonna be chatting with.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.020
And it doesn't matter
if they're on Android

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.720
or if they want to do the
FaceTime chat on their PC,

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.480
in a browser, like this is huge.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.190
The fact that Apple was opening this up

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.180
to just like not just Apple.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.560
Pretty excited about that.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.300
I feel like they're gonna be targeting

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.210
that work from home environment.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.290
I wish that they would have had this

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.680
about a year-and-a-half ago.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.800
But hey, I'm here for it.
We're all here for it.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.730
And I think it's gonna make a
lot of these conference calls

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:06.880
so much more seamless.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.350
SharePlay is another really
cool new feature at FaceTime,

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.070
where you're gonna be able to
listen to music, watch movies,

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.970
TV shows, all together.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.581
And then you're gonna
be able to use AirPlay

00:03:15.581 --> 00:03:18.730
to actually take whatever
that high quality content is

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:19.970
and share it to your TV.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.720
So not only will you be
able to be FaceTiming

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.570
and watching this content simultaneously,

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.440
but you'll be able to
transfer it to your TV

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.640
and be able to watch it in
a higher-quality fashion.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.220
I've actually never
watched content like this

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.120
with anybody else, but I think
it'll be cool to try it out.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.220
I'm very excited about some
of the iMessage updates.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.140
I love this new collage design.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.990
This is gonna give you an
all new way to share content.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.820
I feel like anytime I'm out
with my friends or my family

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:44.830
and we're at an event,

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:47.340
we're always sharing pictures
and photos from that.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.320
So what's gonna be cool,

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.890
is you're gonna be able to
have all of those photos

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.350
in this little collage view.

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.020
And now they're gonna be having this thing

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:57.030
where you can actually have
these photos automatically

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.590
be added to your library.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.890
So you're not gonna have to
save them all individually,

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.230
it'll automatically be added.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.300
And this is what they're calling

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.270
the "Shared with you," with you section.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.940
So not only will this be in photos

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.540
but it'll also be available in music.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.290
And you'll get a list of all of the links

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.450
that people have shared with you.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.950
And this is seriously so cool,

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:17.380
because I use iMessage so
much for this type of thing.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:21.720
Not only for food
recommendations for restaurants,

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.880
but news articles or very
important things that I'm like,

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.610
"You sent me this, but
where the heck is it?"

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.610
They have an updated notification summary

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.890
with various graphics and memojis.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.343
But this is something that's cool:

00:04:33.343 --> 00:04:35.040
They have this new Focus Mode.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.890
So if you are in focus, Work Mode,

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:39.670
you will only receive notifications

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.180
from your co-workers
or Slack notifications.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.080
So you're able to dictate
what mode you're in.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.340
So if you're at home

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.550
you can maybe get notifications
from your friends or family

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.690
but not get co-worker notifications.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:55.120
I love this kind of separation
from work and home life,

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.810
but I, unfortunately I
don't really have that.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.760
It all just blends into one.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.067
It's like, "Oh, did you
want to have a weekend?"

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.107
"What's a weekend?"

00:05:03.107 --> 00:05:05.113
"We don't really have those."

00:05:05.113 --> 00:05:07.810
We have some new intelligent
features like LiveText.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.830
So if you take a photo of a whiteboard

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.120
that will automatically
be translated into text.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.430
So you can basically copy
and paste that whiteboard

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.830
and paste that as text into an email.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.390
It's also taking all of the
texts in all of these photos

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:21.040
and making everything searchable.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.740
They've updated the new photo memories:

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.210
You can choose different songs

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:28.140
and it'll re-edit those little
AI edited movies for you.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.500
I think that this is a very easy thing;

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.080
If there's a face that
you no longer want to see

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.540
in your or memories,

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.190
I feel like you should be able to say,

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:37.287
have check a button that says,

00:05:37.287 --> 00:05:39.000
"I never want you to see this face again."

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.140
Really? Is that so hard?

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.590
All of these incredible features.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.260
Can we please, just get that one

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:46.770
for the sake of many people's
sanity and well-being.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.950
It would be great. I would
love that. Thank you.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.710
There's an update to
Wallet which will allow you

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:55.180
to have access to car keys, hotel keys.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.820
Basically have auto check-in.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:57.847
You'll pick up your phone and you're like,

00:05:57.847 --> 00:06:00.320
"Oh look, there's my room
key, I'm already checked in."

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.910
That is something that I'm excited about.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.480
There's just something about confrontation

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:06.170
that I really don't like when
checking into at a hotel.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.030
It's always just like an ordeal.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.610
But I do like checking in

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.490
when they give you a free little
snack or a bottle of water.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.030
I think I'd rather just
go straight to my room.

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:15.430
You can put the water in there

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:16.610
and I don't have to see anyone.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:18.260
Have I mentioned I'm an introvert?

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:22.200
Digital identity is something
that I'm a huge fan of.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:26.150
I do feel like this is gonna
be the future of identity

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.580
and carrying cards.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.560
I think that's a whole nother conversation

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.610
to talk about how
important the blockchain is

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:34.400
to be able to allow us to
have this digital identity.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.330
And, do you guys hear that?

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.600
Can you hear that or am I just hearing it?

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:40.090
There's a small child
upstairs (table pounds)

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:42.640
stomping her little tiny feet. (giggles)

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.700
Anyway, blockchain technology,

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.380
merging that with digital identity,

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.870
I think is gonna be really
huge in the upcoming years.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.390
But they are doing a little first leap

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.100
into that with us here having the ability

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.780
to scan our driver's licenses

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.060
and be able to potentially
use this at TSA.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.150
I hope that they make it easy

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:01.650
to update your driver's
license with the DMV,

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:06.330
because that place is,
it's yeah, I don't like it.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.510
They've got a new design
for the Weather app.

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:11.380
There's some new graphics to
better understand conditions

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.320
like the wind UV barometric pressure.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.667
I mean, I really just usually say,

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:18.190
"Hey Siri, what's the weather,"
and then she tells me.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.080
AirPods is something that
I was so excited about.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.582
I was hoping, just fingers crossed,

00:07:22.582 --> 00:07:25.430
that they maybe were gonna
announce some new air pods.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:28.900
I just love the first
edition of the AirPods.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.410
These are still my absolute favorite.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.320
But they did announce a new little feature

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.710
that will be helping people
who are hearing impaired.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.080
It's called a Conversation Boost,

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.100
so you can have them in

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.870
and it'll be able to
elevate the conversation

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:39.890
that's happening around you.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:40.740
That's pretty awesome,

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.590
because a lot of people just
wear AirPods all the time

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.580
to take calls or get notifications

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.310
and out we can actually
help you hear more.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.510
So that's pretty cool.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.560
This was also very exciting.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.770
Of course, the AirTags came out

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:55.700
and using the Proximity
Feature with the AirTags,

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.090
you're just able to walk around your house

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.020
and find your item.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.937
But now they're gonna be
integrating that into the AirPods.

00:08:00.937 --> 00:08:02.530
And of course, you'll be
able to play the sound

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:03.363
to try to find them.

00:08:03.363 --> 00:08:05.100
But now adding the proximity support

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.750
is going to be really cool.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.100
I can never freaking
find my AirPods, ever.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.810
Spatial Audio with the AirPods
Max and the AirPods Pro

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:14.450
is just such an incredible thing.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:15.850
It's cool because
they're now bringing this

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.810
to tvOS and Mac iOS with the M1 Chip,

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.170
so that'll be really cool to try.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:22.470
There's a bunch of new iPad OS updates,

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.100
like new widgets on the home screen.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.660
There's a new Find My in Contact Widgets.

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:28.090
There's new game center widgets.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.370
They've also made it easier to reorganize

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:31.210
a lot of your apps.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.230
So the app library,

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:36.170
you're able to relocate
entire pages or hide those,

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:38.140
so that they're no
longer on your homepage.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.540
There's a new Multitasking Menu

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.630
and they've made it so much
easier to do split screen.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.560
I do feel like sometimes
for whatever reason

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.410
I always try to do split screen on my iPad

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.070
and I either do it wrong
or it doesn't look right.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.880
So I love this little demo that they did

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:52.890
to show how easy it is to
start a new split screen.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.860
You can just drag and drop
one of the apps onto another

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:57.460
and it's like, boom, automatic!

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.710
There's also updates coming to Notes.

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:01.360
And I'm such a huge Notes fan,

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.390
I use this to write all of my scripts.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:05.000
Right now, I have all of the notes

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.950
from the WWDC event written here.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.420
And it's so easy because you can just

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:09.520
share these notes directly.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:12.350
But they've started adding a
few new things like Mentions,

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:14.250
which can be really great
for me and my sister,

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.690
and Tyler also, because
when we do the podcast

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:20.130
we will do all of our notes
inside of the Notes app.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:21.972
So we'll be able to mention,

00:09:21.972 --> 00:09:23.910
"Hey Tyler, do you think
this is a good idea?"

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:25.420
Or, "Hey, Jenna, make sure you do this."

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:26.790
There's also hashtags.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.810
There's also an activity
view so you'll be able to see

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:30.040
the things that have changed.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.300
And I'll even have Quick Notes,

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.480
so you'll be able to use your Apple Pencil

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.070
and just swipe from the corner
and just start taking notes.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.000
And those will also all be
available right in the Notes app.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.870
I love the Notes app. It's the best.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:44.100
Obviously privacy is such a huge concern.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.490
I mean, we are sharing
so much of our lives

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:48.840
and personal information
on all of these devices.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:52.410
So I love that Apple is really
spearheading all of this

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.640
to make sure that we are being safe.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.700
So they announced an
update for the Mail app,

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.280
which will give us the option
to hide our IP addresses.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.530
'Cause they were talking about
a lot of these spam emails

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:03.570
can tell if you open it,

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:06.620
because they have these
invisible little graphics

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.860
and all kinds of things in
them to be able to track you,

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:10.030
to get your IP address,

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:12.290
and then track you all
over the freaking web.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.200
Like, get out of my business!

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:18.130
They've also announced
that there is an iCloud+.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:20.700
This will be we able to use Safari

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.820
to do a private relay browsing.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:25.800
So this is gonna be adding a
whole nother level of security.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:26.780
So if you do want to sign up

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:30.240
for some newsletter or something,
you can hide your email.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.190
So you can create endless amounts

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.330
of different email addresses,

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:37.320
and then have them forwarded
to your actual email address.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.440
And if you want to delete
one of those email addresses

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.960
you can easily do that too.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:43.580
They also talked about
HomeKit Secure Video.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.950
You can receive, like if
a package or something

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.020
is delivered to your door,

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.480
you'll get a package notification.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.040
And I was just thinking
of the amount of packages

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:51.520
that I receive on a daily basis;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:52.770
my phone is just gonna be like,

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:54.350
ding, ding, ding ding, ding.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.580
Just always exciting
when I get a fun package.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.170
But yeah, definitely
want to test that out.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:02.310
They also announced a new way
to recover your iCloud account

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.870
if you're unable to access it.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.920
So you can add trusted people

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:08.350
who will not have access
to your iCloud account,

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.400
but they will be an added trusted person

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:14.000
that can call and retrieve
a number or a PIN number,

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.240
and then you have to enter that

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.440
so that you can get
back into your account.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.890
Along that same note of iCloud recovery,

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:20.620
they added Legacy Accounts.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.330
If someone passes away,

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.780
you'll be able to designate

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.890
who can have access to your information

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:27.140
and then what to do with it.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:30.560
And it's really a terrible
thing to think about,

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:33.120
but I'm really, really glad
that they're doing this.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.500
They talked a lot about health

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:38.080
and I love the fact that
Apple is very health focused.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.870
Obviously with the Apple Watch,

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.710
this has so many health
features built into it,

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:43.830
but it is surprising how
much has actually built

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.103
into the iPhone.

00:11:45.103 --> 00:11:49.010
They have this new Walking
Steadiness Feature.

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:51.090
So it will be able to recognize

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:53.940
and determine your walking trends.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.130
And along these sort of same lines,

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.460
they've got another new feature

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.320
where you're able to share
your health with someone.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.960
This is gonna be very
helpful for I feel like,

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.440
if we want our parents to be able

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.950
to share their health data with us.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.930
So you get a notification
when one of your parents

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.690
may have a lower heart rate
or a higher heart rate.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:13.660
Or if they're walking steadiness declines

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:14.977
you'll be able to get a notification that,

00:12:14.977 --> 00:12:16.680
"Hey, something's going on,

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:18.480
maybe you should check on so-and-so."

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.570
Some updates in watch OS:
They have two new workouts.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:24.070
There's a Pilates and a Tai-Chi workout.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:27.680
I love that a really been
integrating new workouts

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:28.700
into the Apple Watch.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.080
I still wish that I could
wear this for jujitsu,

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.930
but they do have a martial
arts option on here.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.150
They didn't officially announce home OS,

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:38.360
but they were talking a lot about HomeKit.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:41.370
I feel like this might be
tying into a separate event.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.790
Hopefully there'll be
something really cool

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:43.960
that they announce for the home.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.380
I did think that maybe we would have heard

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.660
a little bit more about this,

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:48.670
but they just we're showing

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:50.610
how everything all works together.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:54.040
Mac OS Monterrey, I cannot
wait to try this out.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.450
I'm very excited about
it because I did just,

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:58.050
ah, Big Sur was so beautiful,

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:00.130
so they're just adding
some updates to this.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:04.410
Now I use multiple devices
all the time so usually

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:07.610
I will have my main
computer, I'll have my iPad,

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.770
and it sometimes I'll even
have my MacBook next to me.

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:11.740
And all of these things, I'm
doing something different,

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:14.050
and they're all still working together.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:18.040
But now, this is probably
honestly one of the best updates

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:21.610
that I've seen at WWDC so
far, of the whole event.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.220
It's called Universal Control.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.740
So if I have my iPad,
my iMac, and my MacBook

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:26.940
all sitting next to each other,

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:30.488
they will automatically act as, I guess,

00:13:30.488 --> 00:13:32.240
like external devices,

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.490
but I can use them all
with the same mouse,

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:36.920
the same keyboard.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.010
So I can use my mouse on my iMac

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.270
and then I can scroll over to my iPad

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:44.100
and then I can be using
my iPad with my mouse

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.880
and I can type and I
can use shortcut keys.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.030
And then I can slide all
the way over to my MacBook

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:50.010
and everything just works seamlessly.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.390
This is freaking cool!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.293
Now I'm just saying it out loud.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.320
This is exciting.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:58.510
Like super excite, like
I'm hyped about this.

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:00.150
And if you guys aren't hyped about it,

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.640
that's fine, it's okay.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.317
Allow me to have this moment.

00:14:03.317 --> 00:14:04.250
(inhales)

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:06.900
To know all of this stuff
that we've talked about today

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.830
is going to be available to developers,

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.400
actually starting today.

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:12.683
One update that I thought was cool

00:14:12.683 --> 00:14:15.010
that they mentioned, that I
forgot to mention earlier,

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:16.820
is an update to Apple Maps.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:21.180
They have this new, I guess
like AR-3D street map view,

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:24.590
where if you're stuck
somewhere and you're lost

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.720
you can basically get
your phone, hold it up,

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.690
and it'll make this whole
augmented reality map

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.700
so it'll show you exactly
where you have to go.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.600
Now I know that Apple Maps,

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.180
it's weird because it's like
a love-hate relationship

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:38.013
that I have with it.

00:14:38.013 --> 00:14:40.720
Apple Maps looks way
better than Google Maps

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:43.360
and I love that Apple Maps
works with my Apple Watch

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.520
so if I'm driving or if I'm on a bike,

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:47.330
it'll give me that haptic feedback

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.410
to let me know that I
have a turn coming up.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.490
But for whatever reason,

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.100
sometimes I don't feel the confidence

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.690
if I have to get somewhere on time,

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.050
I usually would go to Google.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:58.890
But I am excited about
some of these updates

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:01.960
because they've really made
Apple Maps look beautiful.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:04.790
And to have this
integration in with CarPlay,

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:05.623
it's gonna be cool.

00:15:05.623 --> 00:15:08.520
They've added so much more
detail in neighborhoods.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.310
They've redesigned the roads.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:13.540
They have custom design
landmarks, elevation,

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:14.940
and so much more.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:16.210
So that was just a little look

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:19.260
at some of the highlights that
were announced here at WWDC.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:22.700
I love this event because
it really does set us up

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:23.730
for the rest of the year.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:25.870
And I can not wait to get my
hands on the beta versions

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:26.703
